.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_NAME_GET0_DER 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_NAME_get0_der
.Nd get X509_NAME DER encoding
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_NAME_get0_der
.Fa "const X509_NAME *nm"
.Fa "const unsigned char **pder"
.Fa "size_t *pderlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The function
.Fn X509_NAME_get0_der
returns an internal pointer to the encoding of an
.Sy X509_NAME
structure in
.Sy *pder
and consisting of
.Sy *pderlen
bytes.
It is useful for applications that wish to examine the encoding of an
.Sy X509_NAME
structure without copying it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The function
.Fn X509_NAME_get0_der
returns 1 for success and 0 if an error occurred.
